- Story & Context: We climbed the emergency ladder to the rusted water cistern above Dadar Terminus, carrying an amateur refractor telescope and three pocket synthesizers taped together with duct tape. When the 01:40 Konkan Express shuddered out of platform four, the vibration knocked the telescope out of alignment and pinned our synth lead on a weeping microtonal bend. As the diesel fumes curled into the smog-hazed constellation of Orion, Aarav cracked an egg over the hot exhaust pipe and Priya leaned into the microphone to hum, "The blue star drowns before our wheels can turn."
