Track 2: Whose Roof Is Touching Jupiter?
- Story & Context: Sunita Rao sat cross-legged on a cracked blue plastic chair atop an unpermitted six-story terrace overlooking the rail junction at Kalyan, her thumbs blistered from manipulating a ribbon-synth controller all night long. She confessed through her vocoder that she had run away from the Pune music conservatory because her gurus forbade her from playing sacred morning ragas over quantized 4/4 kicks. With Jupiter hanging like an unblinking copper bead beside the rooftop television aerials, she let the synth bass shake the loose roof tiles while crying into her tea, repeating the hook, "Ask the planet if my tempo is a sin."
