Track 3: Patri-Bhairavi (Sleeper-Tala)
- Story & Context: Legend says that during a track derailment near the Igatpuri viaduct in the monsoon of 2017, five stranded commuters left a battery sequencer looping an infinite Bhairavi bassline directly into the railway's steel guardrail. Roof-dwellers and amateur stargazers on the mountain crest miles away placed their ears against lightning rods and discovered the valley was humming in perfect modal accord with the morning fog. By the time the repair locomotive arrived with clanking chains and smelling of bitter tea, the valley had learned the melody by heart, leaving behind only the distant vocoder refrain, "Sing to the cold rail until daylight breaks the spell."
